    "sections": [
      {
        "h2": "How to Match Foundation Shades Accurately to Skin Undertones?",
        "content": "<p>To match foundation accurately, swatch two to three candidate shades along your lower jawline down onto your neck in natural outdoor lighting, selecting the shade that disappears seamlessly into the skin.</p>\n          <p>Identify your underlying undertone before testing shades:</p>\n          <ul>\n            <li><strong>Warm Undertones:</strong> Skin features golden, peachy, or yellow casts; look for warm (W) labeled foundations.</li>\n            <li><strong>Cool Undertones:</strong> Skin features pink, red, or bluish hints; choose cool (C) foundation formulas.</li>\n            <li><strong>Neutral Undertones:</strong> Skin displays an even balance between yellow and pink tones; select neutral (N) foundation bottles.</li>\n          </ul>"
      },
      {
        "h2": "What Techniques Prevent Makeup from Creasing or Separating in Humid Climates?",
        "content": "<p>Preventing makeup separation during humid Tarai weather requires oil-free priming, applying foundation in sheer micro-layers, and pressing translucent setting powder into high-movement areas using a damp sponge.</p>\n          <p>Avoid rubbing foundation with dry fingers, as friction creates uneven patches and warms facial oils prematurely. Finish with a fine mist of setting spray to seal pigments against sweat and humidity.</p>"
      },
      {
        "h2": "How to Select and Inspect Genuine Makeup Products in Itahari?",
        "content": "<p>Mastering color matching and blending technique is most rewarding when cosmetic formulations are physically inspected for batch freshness and shade fidelity before purchasing.</p>\n          <p>Individual beauty enthusiasts in Eastern Nepal can explore our complete collection of <a href=\"/cosmetics/makeup/\">Makeup Products in Itahari, Nepal</a> at our Janta Galli storefront with transparent 5% savings on MRP, while local retailers can order custom mixed cartons for their beauty counters.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "q": "How can I prevent foundation from looking cakey or heavy?",
        "a": "Apply foundation in sheer dots starting from the center of the face outward, buffing with a damp sponge rather than applying a thick single layer."
      },
      {
        "q": "What is the difference between setting powder and compact powder?",
        "a": "Translucent setting powder absorbs surface oil and fixes foundation without adding color, whereas compact powder adds coverage and pigment."
      }
    ]
